Keep exactly one task `active`. Each slice must have an observable result and a verification command or artifact before it starts. Use only `not_started`, `active`, `blocked`, `verified`, and `passing` for task state.

## Checkpoints

At each checkpoint, record the decision, changed files, verification command and exit status, remaining risk, and the next slice. A failed check moves the slice back to `active` and records the failure.

## Closeout

The plan is complete only after local verification, a draft GitHub PR, required CI checks, the final commit and PR URL, and the corresponding tracking and handoff updates are recorded.

Push and PR actions require authorization in the current task; preserve any authorization already given. Use the documented harness deliver command to record actual remote/CI evidence.
